    "result_text": "I've implemented `build_client` in `app/llm_client.py`. `pytest -q` passes, and a separate check with a stub transport showed all four requirements working.\n\n**How it works:**\n- It builds the HTTP client with the openai SDK's `DefaultHttpxClient`, so the SDK's defaults (connection limits, following redirects) stay in place.\n- **Timeouts:** 5 seconds to connect, 30 seconds for read, write and pool. They're set on both the HTTP client and the `OpenAI` client, because the SDK sends its own timeout with every request.\n- **Retries:** `max_retries=2`.\n- **Logging:** an event hook on the HTTP client logs `\"<METHOD> <URL>\"` at INFO on the `app.http` logger. The hook runs on every request, including each retry.\n- **Transport:** passed straight to the HTTP client. When it's `None`, the normal default transport is used.\n\n**What the check showed:** I made the stub return a 500 on the first call and a 200 on the second, then called `client.models.list()`. That made 2 requests (the original plus one retry), and each was logged as `app.http INFO GET https://api.openai.com/v1/models`. The client and each request both had timeouts of connect 5.0, read/write/pool 30.0.\n\nI wasn't allowed to delete the temporary script `_check.py` in the project root, so please remove it yourself. I didn't add or install any dependencies: `httpx` already comes with `openai`."
